#!/bin/sh
# Pre-commit checks. `bun install` enables this hook through the `prepare`
# script (git config core.hooksPath .githooks). CI runs the same checks, plus
# the tests and the dist/ check, on every push and pull request.
#
# Prettier and ESLint see only the staged files; the other checks are
# project-wide but take a few seconds. They read the working tree, so stage
# the full content of a file before committing it.
set -eu

cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"

run() {
  echo "pre-commit: $*"
  "$@"
}

staged() {
  git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR -z -- "$@"
}

if [ -n "$(staged | tr -d '\0')" ]; then
  staged | xargs -0 bun x --bun prettier --check --ignore-unknown
fi

if [ -n "$(staged '*.ts' '*.js' '*.mjs' '*.cjs' | tr -d '\0')" ]; then
  staged '*.ts' '*.js' '*.mjs' '*.cjs' |
    xargs -0 bun x --bun eslint --no-warn-ignored
fi

run bun run --silent typecheck
run bun run --silent check:static

echo 'pre-commit: all checks passed'
